Source reference: 7f2fc0d (main), as recorded in docs/rayneo-protocol.md.

Adapted protocol framing/CRC, protobuf/TLV format, guest BLE authentication,
RFCOMM service selection, caption display handshake/full-width alignment,
Opus MediaCodec setup and TOC timing from:
  android/.../ProtocolCodec.kt
  android/.../RayneoConnection.kt
  android/.../GlassesDisplay.kt
  android/.../PromptAudio.kt
  Sources/OpenRayneoBridge/main.swift
  Sources/OpenRayneoBridge/DisplayController.swift

The post-discovery/first-MTU callback gate is adapted from the Apache-2.0
OpenRayneo fork by ruchirlives, reference 1943b92 (android-english-voice),
android/.../BleIdentityGate.kt. Its repository inherits the upstream license.
Upstream fork: https://github.com/ruchirlives/OpenRayneo

Modified for RayNeo iO HUD: Kotlin transport lifecycle, bounded coroutine write queue,
reconnect policy, minimal protobuf support, command/event APIs, setup UI,
frame pacing, unsupported character handling, PCM downsampling and tests.
Preserved source copyright/SPDX headers identify adapted Kotlin files.

The full Apache-2.0 license is provided in LICENSE-OpenRayneo and in APK assets
as openrayneo-license.txt; this notice is also in APK assets.
No Turbo-IO implementation code or modified firmware is included.
Android's platform MediaCodec supplies the Opus decoder; no Opus library is vendored.

